revision.text:
The '''Sigil Advisory Council''' is a civilian organization, set up in the wake of the [[Faction War]], which ostensibly runs [[Sigil]] in the absence of the [[Faction]]s.

== History ==
As [[Rhys]]<ref name="ettdp14">{{b|D&D|Expedition to the Demonweb Pits|pdf=54341|nip=1|page=14}}</ref> was the only surviving [[factol]] in the wake of the War, and given the [[Transcendent Order]] had always encouraged other factions to solve disagreements with diplomacy, the Order tore up their charter so they could stay in Sigil, and help Cagers set up the Sigil Advisory Council.

The Council has nine seats, including the only one with previous government experience: Rhys herself. Although officially she has no more power than any other representative, she's afforded a great deal of respect. 

One of their first duties was to order the [[Hall of Records]] locked, since the newly-empty building was being pillaged. By the time it was locked, however, it was too late, so the slate had been wiped clean for most Cagers.

== Role ==

While the elected officials typically revel in the cachet associated with being an Official Councilor, they do genuinely attempt to work for the betterment of Sigil. Unfortunately they have little way of enforcing their rulings, so most of Sigil's residents don't perceive them as having a lot of power. They haven't been torn to shreds by the Lady, so they may have more authority than Cagers think.

The Council does engage in charitable efforts, particularly in the more upscale parts of the city, and will sometimes hire adventurers to deal with problems. They also occasionally work with the [[Mutual Trade Association]] to help push forth edicts and get things done.

